\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{The index in a gauge field}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{How do gauge transformations, reflection and charge conjugation act on the
overlap index? Which connections have index zero? When the links commute pairwise,
how does the index split over their characters? For any unitary connection in dimension
#{n\ge 2}, which integer do the links give on a closed surface of [plain plaquettes](fdip-015V)?
When #{n\ge 3}, how does the cancellation on the boundaries of the cubes in a closed
chain compare with that for Hermitian symbols in \ref{fdip-015Q}?}

\p{The statements hold for any dimension #{n\ge 1}, any periods #{N_j\ge 3}, any Hermitian
Clifford module with a grading and any unitary connection, unless a statement names a
restriction.}
